43
00:02:02,400 --> 00:02:09,760
All right, so this first one is an important one because generally when you're looking for a house or an apartment, there are two things you can do.

44
00:02:09,760 --> 00:02:14,340
You can buy a house or you can lease a house or apartment.

45
00:02:14,760 --> 00:02:16,120
So lease here, Marco.

46
00:02:16,620 --> 00:02:18,640
It's basically to rent, right?

47
00:02:19,140 --> 00:02:27,080
It's a contract where you agree to pay a monthly or a quarterly fee for using that house or apartment.

48
00:02:27,080 --> 00:02:28,840
So do you own your apartment or do you lease it?

49
00:02:29,240 --> 00:02:30,460
No, mine, I lease.

50
00:02:30,840 --> 00:02:32,460
I am not a homeowner yet.

51
00:02:32,860 --> 00:02:33,020
Right.

52
